# (AI-assisted) performance measurement: the gameplay.pad route with fixed idle windows between
# "perf-mark" log lines, so every run measures the same scenes over the same frames. Summarize a
# run with platform/3ds/tools/perf_report.py <stdout.log>. Windows (game frames):
#   title      600 frames on the title screen (village1 in the background)
#   menu       600 frames in the title menu (progress), nothing pressed
#   newgame    New Game: menu taps, loading village1 (the "intro" continue)
#   intro      the intro cutscene before it is skipped
#   skip       skipping the intro, loading
#   idle       1800 frames: Jak idle in village1 (intro-start, where Jak lands after the intro)
#   moves      walking, jumping, attacks (gameplay.pad's moves)
#   idle2      1800 frames idle after the moves (the scene of the older "after done" numbers)
